# Add jsdom environment to Vitest configuration

Scenario: happyPath
Model: deepseek-v4-flash
Generated: 2026-05-30T08:42:27.559Z
Stale conflict recovered: no

Update `vite.config.ts` to set the test environment to `jsdom`:

```typescript
import { defineConfig } from 'vite';
import react from '@vitejs/plugin-react';

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [react()],
  test: {
    globals: true,
    environment: 'jsdom',
  },
});
```

This aligns with the smoke acceptance criteria and ensures DOM APIs are available for testing.

## Problem
Stale write occurs when a patch preview is based on old DOM state. If the task item structure changes after preview, applying the patch may corrupt the DOM.

## Fix
Add a version attribute to task items and validate it before toggling completion.

### Changes in `src/taskBoard.ts`:
```typescript
// Inside addTask method, add data-version:
const version = Date.now();
taskItem.dataset.version = String(version);

// In toggleCompletion method:
const expectedVersion = taskItem.dataset.version;
const currentDOM = document.querySelector(`[data-task-id="${taskId}"][data-version="${expectedVersion}"]`);
if (!currentDOM) {
  console.warn('Stale write detected, skipping toggle');
  return;
}
// Proceed with toggle logic...
```

### Verification
Run `npm run test:run` and ensure all five smoke tests pass. The fix prevents stale writes without breaking existing functionality.

